r-r-refused. No field holds this.\n- **Lowest acceptable amount:** it is the higher of the product's base minimum and a quarter of the overdue sum (rounded up to the cent), but never more than the full sum. This is stored in `floor_rules` with extra keys (`min_field`, `combine_with_field`, `rounding`, `cap`).\n\nThe policy schema accepts these extra keys, but the compiler won't apply them unless it is made to read them."}
{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "31d3b14f2dfc4148b77a8a40a4d05b40", "pid": 103191, "time": "2026-10-10T20:11:05-0700", "elapsed_s": 169.613, "artifact": "out/ext-cedar.policy.json", "bands": 1, "identity_fields": ["birth_date", "access_pin", "locality_word"], "special_cases": ["already_paid", "dispute", "hardship", "restructuring", "human", "scam", "refuse_to_talk"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "bands.CR-D1.deadline", "text": "Deadline is the EARLIER of (a) the sixth business day strictly after today and (b) the last business day of the current calendar month; neither boundary may be exceeded. The DSL has no min-of-two rule, so the deadline is encoded as nth_business_day n=6 with an extra 'cap' (end_of_month, business basis, current month) and combine='earlier'; the compiler must apply the cap.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}, {"topic": "bands.CR-D1.deadline_before_today", "text": "If the deadline is already before today, no eligible promise date exists: take no promise and close cr-none/cr-r-refused; never extend into the following month. No IR field expresses this.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}, {"topic": "amounts.floor_rules", "text": "Effective floor = min(full overdue sum, max(product base field [flex_base/term_base], ceil-to-cent(25% of full overdue sum))). The API base fields are not the final floor; the DSL has no combined field+percent rule, so floor_rules carry extra keys min_field, combine_with_field='higher', rounding='up_to_cent', cap='full_amount' that the compiler must honour. Do not use the base alone or round to nearest.", "doc": "sources/000-01-specification.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["Removed unresolved entry 'identity.wrong_count': the document settles it (count in agent code, 4 total) and it is already expressed by identity.wrong_count_source='code' and wrong_answer_limit=4.", "Added 'A relative cannot verify or promise for the holder.' to third_party.source so that rule is traceable.", "Extended amounts.source and promise_write.source with the below-floor, no-discount, consent-revalidation and service-failure sentences for traceability; no values changed.", "Verified all other values against the specification and openapi enums (verify_identity field, close_call outcome/reason, transfer_to_agent queue, contract_kind); no value errors found."], "audit_unresolved": ["CR-D1 deadline is the earlier of two rules (6th business day vs last business day of current month); the DSL has no min-of-two, encoded with extra 'cap'/'combine' keys the compiler must honour.", "Deadline-before-today case (no promise, close cr-none/cr-r-refused) has no IR field.", "Effective floor combines a base field, a 25% rule rounded up to the cent, and a cap at full; the floor_rules DSL cannot express it natively, encoded with extra keys."], "defaulted_without_source": []}
